<article class="env-lemma" id="0C29">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C29">Lemma <span data-tag="0C29">15.110.2</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. The number of branches of $A$ is the same as the number of branches of $A^\wedge $ if and only if $\sqrt{\mathfrak qA^\wedge }$ is prime for every minimal prime $\mathfrak q \subset A^ h$ of the henselization. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0C28" data-tag="0C28">15.110.1</a> and the fact that there are only a finite number of branches for both $A$ and $A^\wedge $ by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00FR" data-tag="00FR">10.31.6</a> and the fact that $A^ h$ and $A^\wedge $ are Noetherian (Lemma <a href="/tag/06LJ" data-tag="06LJ">15.46.3</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>